Subject: [PATCH 06969/11362] Task 10: REQ-ARC-FCP-5591-2 spec + real exp5601
 empirical validation (change-history signal CONFIRMED on real m0r0 play)

Adds REQ-ARC-FCP-5591-2 and its five SCENARIOs to
openspec/capabilities/arc-human-replay-frame-change/spec.md, documenting
ObjectHistorySaliencePrior's contract and the empirical-validation gate task
10's DONE note deferred.

Ran the real exp5601 offline-sim prototype against m0r0 (confirmed
click-heavy by exp5595): 37 real transitions collected, 32 clicks, 15
distinct object_hash identities tracked. 2 hashes cleared the
min_observations=3 evidence floor, and BOTH show a nonzero real change rate
-- honest_verdict=complete: object_history_salience_prototype_confirmed_2_
hashes_with_real_change_signal_across_1_games. The adversarial degeneracy
sub-check found 0 of 8 same-base-tier real candidate pairs diverging in
observed history within this specific 37-transition sample (an honest
limitation of sample size for that sub-check, not a failure of the
mechanism -- the synthetic unit test already proves differentiation is
possible when history does diverge).

duration_s=34.0, inference_substrate=offline_arcade_live_agent_runtime_
self_discovery_no_llm (a real LocalGGUFProposer is constructed to avoid the
bare-construction stall but never invoked -- pure classical exploration).
8 tests (including a real-artifact-reading test matching the exp5591/5595
convention) all pass.

SUBMITTED_OBJECT_HISTORY_SALIENCE_ENABLED stays False -- this confirms the
mechanism has real signal to act on, not that it's safe to enable for the
scored agent (that needs its own matched-budget A/B, per the
solve_rate_dropped guardrail).

